Code Meaning <code>0</code> Command completed; a scan can be partial unless <code>--strict</code> was requested <code>1</code> At least one unsuppressed finding met <code>--fail-on</code> <code>2</code> Fatal command, configuration, platform, input or output error <code>3</code> Strict-mode scan had incomplete collection; the report was still written <code>130</code> Interrupted scan/command where interruption is reported <p>Fatal errors take precedence. When both strict incompleteness and a severity threshold apply, exit 3 takes precedence. Suppressed findings remain in the report but do not trigger <code>--fail-on</code>. A daemon normally exits 0 on graceful SIGTERM.</p> <p>Shell example that preserves the scanner's status:</p> <pre><code>status=0
lasa scan --strict --fail-on high --format json --output host.report.json || status=$?
case "$status" in
  0) echo 'scan completed within selected acceptance policy' ;;
  1) echo 'review severity threshold findings' ;;
  3) echo 'review incomplete coverage before interpreting findings' ;;
  *) echo "command failed with status $status" &gt;&amp;2; exit "$status" ;;
esac
</code></pre>
